    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12">
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Malaysia's electronics manufacturing belt — Penang, Kulim, Klang Valley — runs on tight ESD discipline. One static spark can destroy a populated PCB or knock an entire batch of memory chips out of spec, and the failure won't appear until end-customer testing. Pink anti-static bubble wrap is the cheapest layer of insurance against this. Quinocycle supplies anti-static wrap from our Balakong stock to PCB assembly houses, semiconductor distributors, and electronics e-tailers across Peninsular Malaysia.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Pink Anti-Static — What It Actually Does</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">The Static Problem in Plain Terms</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">When two surfaces rub together — including the inside of standard plastic bubble wrap moving against itself — they exchange electrons and build up static charge. A finger touching a sensitive IC can deliver 5,000-15,000 volts in a single discharge. The chip sees nothing visible, but its silicon junctions are now compromised. Pink anti-static wrap blocks this at the surface level by being mildly conductive — charge dissipates instead of building up.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Where Pink Sits in the ESD Hierarchy</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Pink anti-static is the workhorse for general electronics packaging. It prevents static generation but does not shield against external ESD. For Class 1 ESDS components (MOSFETs, CMOS, EPROM), pair pink bubble wrap with metallised shielding bags. For Class 2 ICs and Class 3 populated boards, pink wrap alone is usually adequate.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Shelf Life Reality</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Anti-static treatment is migratory — the agent gradually evaporates and effectiveness declines after 12-24 months. We rotate stock so what ships from Balakong has at least 12 months of effective life remaining. The manufacture date is printed on every roll for your traceability.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Common Use Cases in Malaysian Electronics</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">PCB Assembly & Inter-Plant Movement</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">EMS factories shuttle WIP boards between SMT, AOI, conformal coat, and final test stations all day. Plain wrap on these movements builds static. Pink wrap rolls feeding semi-automatic cushioning machines on the line eliminate this risk at minor incremental cost.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Semiconductor Distribution</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Distributors holding chip inventory in Bayan Lepas, Subang, and Petaling Jaya use pink wrap as the secondary cushion inside shipper cartons containing reels and trays. The original anti-static bag handles ESD shielding; pink wrap protects against physical impact during last-mile delivery.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">E-Commerce Electronics Sellers</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Shopee and Lazada sellers pushing graphics cards, RAM modules, motherboards, and SSDs need anti-static wrap to maintain warranty conditions. Most manufacturer warranties are voided if static damage is detected — pink wrap in transit packaging keeps you on the right side of the claim.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Spec & Sizing Guide</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">For PCBs and small components, 10mm bubble height in 500mm-wide rolls is standard. For larger boards, motherboards, and assembled units, step up to 25mm bubble in 1000mm rolls. Length options range from 50m for low-volume operations to 100m+ industrial rolls for production lines. We can pre-cut sheets to your most common board sizes if it saves operator time on the line.</p>
      </section>

